Here's a simple Java method to reverse a linked list:

```java
public class LinkedList {
    public static Node reverseList(Node head) {
        Node prev = null;
        Node current = head;
        Node next = null;

        while (current != null) {
            next = current.next;
            current.next = prev;
            prev = current;
            current = next;
        }

        return prev;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Node head = new Node(1);
        head.next = new Node(2);
        head.next.next = new Node(3);
        head.next.next.next = new Node(4);

        Node reversedHead = reverseList(head);

        while (reversedHead != null) {
            System.out.print(reversedHead.data + " ");
            reversedHead = reversedHead.next;
        }
    }
}
```

This method uses a two-pointer approach, where the `prev` pointer points to the last node in the list, and the `current` pointer points to the first node. It then iterates through the list, reversing the `next` pointers of each node

The async keyword in JavaScript is used to define a function that can run in parallel with other functions. It allows you to write asynchronous code that can handle multiple tasks concurrently.

Here's an example:

```javascript
async function myFunction() {
  // Simulate some asynchronous work
  console.log("Async work started");
  await someAsyncOperation();
  console.log("Async work completed");
}

async function someAsyncOperation() {
  // Simulate some asynchronous work
  console.log("Async work started");
  await someAsyncAwait();
  console.log("Async work completed");
}

async function someAsyncAwait() {
  // Simulate some asynchronous work
  console.log("Async work started");
  await someAsyncOperation();
  console.log("Async work completed");
}

myFunction();
```

In this example, `myFunction` is an async function that runs in parallel with `someAsyncOperation` and `someAsyncAwait`. The `await` keyword is used to pause the execution of the async function until the asynchronous operation completes.

You can also use async functions with promises
